\section{Layout constants}

The header occupies row~0 and the footer the last row, leaving the
content area in between.  We name those offsets so the draw chunks
read as layout statements rather than arithmetic.
[[SHORT_HASH_LEN]] is [[render]]'s, not a second copy: the short hash
in the raw header and the one in a card's \enquote{go back to this
version} hint have to be the same hash, or the student copies a prefix
from one place that does not name what the other showed.

<<viewer constants>>=
HEADER_ROW = 0
CONTENT_START_ROW = 1
FOOTER_OFFSET_FROM_BOTTOM = 2
@

Two more constants belong to the drawing rather than the layout.
[[DEFAULT_PAGE]] is what a page-key press moves before the first draw
has measured the window---no real keypress can arrive that early,
since [[_main_loop]] draws before it reads, but a unit test drives
[[_handle_key]] with no screen at all and must still get a defined
step.
[[FILTERED_NOTE]] is the one line a commit gets when
[[get_commit_detail]] filtered every run block out of it; it names the
flag that brings the commit back, because a reader who meets the note
is by definition looking for what is missing.

<<viewer constants>>=
DEFAULT_PAGE = 20
FILTERED_NOTE = (
    "(learnlog's own setup \u2014 hidden; "
    "use --all to see it)"
)
