The content is whatever [[render]] makes of this record, and the
viewer's whole contribution to it is the three facts only a viewer
knows: where the record sits in the list, how long the student paused
before it, and which tags name it.
The [[Time since last run:]] line the viewer used to prepend by hand
is gone from here---the card carries it among its own meta lines
(\cref{sec:record-lines}), which is what makes the pause read as part
of the record instead of a note stuck on top of it, and what keeps
batch mode from having to prepend the same line a second way.

A commit whose every run block was filtered away has no card to build,
so it gets the one dim line that says so.

<<build content lines>>=
if detail is None:
    content_lines = [StyledLine(FILTERED_NOTE, KIND_DIM)]
else:
    content_lines = record_lines(
        commit, detail,
        index=self.index,
        total=len(self.commits),
